## 3. Booking Procedures

### 3.1 Flight Bookings

**Class of Travel:**

| Route | Class | Exceptions |
|-------|-------|-----------|
| **Domestic (India), <3 hours** | Economy | None |
| **Domestic, >3 hours** | Economy | VP+ can book Business (pre-approval required) |
| **International (South Asia)** | Economy | Senior roles (VP+) can book Business |
| **International (Rest of World)** | Economy | Business/Premium for flights >5 hours (VP+ pre-approval) |

**Booking Timeline:**
- Book domestic flights **at least 5 working days** in advance to secure better fares
- Book international flights **at least 2 weeks** in advance
- Last-minute bookings (within 24 hours) require VP approval and should be exceptions

**Preferred Airlines:**
- IndiGo, SpiceJet, GoAir (for domestic budget options)
- Air India, Vistara (full-service carriers; preferred for long flights)
- International: Partner airlines negotiated by the company; booking team will provide list

**Booking Process:**
- Use the company's preferred travel portal or approved travel agency
- Employees should NOT book personal airlines or unauthorized travel providers
- For reimbursement purposes, only receipts from approved vendors are processed

**Flight Cancellation Insurance:**
- Company will cover cancellation insurance for non-refundable tickets (typically 1–3% of ticket cost)
- Employees should add cancellation insurance when booking

### 3.2 Hotel Bookings

**Budget Guidelines:**

| City | Daily Rate (Accommodation + Breakfast) |
|------|----------------------------------------|
| **Tier 1 Cities (Delhi, Mumbai, Bangalore, Hyderabad)** | Up to INR 10,000 |
| **Tier 2 Cities (Pune, Jaipur, Ahmedabad, Chandigarh)** | Up to INR 6,000 |
| **Tier 3 Cities** | Up to INR 4,000 |
| **International (SAARC)** | USD 120–150 per night |
| **International (Rest of World)** | USD 200–250 per night |

**Hotel Standards:**
- 3-star or equivalent
- Within a reasonable distance of business location (max 20 km)
- Safe and reputable properties with good reviews (minimum 4-star rating on TripAdvisor/Google)

**Booking Process:**
- Use the company's corporate travel portal for negotiated rates
- Alternatively, book 2–3 star hotels on OYO, MakeMyTrip, or other approved portals
- Email confirmation and booking receipt should be retained

**Cancellation Policy:**
- Book hotels with flexible cancellation policy (free cancellation up to 24 hours before)
- If plans change, cancel immediately to avoid charges

### 3.3 Ground Transportation

**Within City:**

| Distance / Situation | Transportation | Budget |
|----------------------|-----------------|--------|
| **Airport to Hotel** | Pre-arranged cab or company cab service | INR 1,500–4,000 (one-way) |
| **City Travel (<10 km)** | Uber/Ola or auto-rickshaw | Actual cost |
| **City Travel (>10 km)** | Uber/Ola (cab, not auto) | Actual cost |
| **Recurring Route (Bangalore–Mumbai)** | Intercity cab service or flight | INR 10,000–15,000 |

**Between Cities:**
- Domestic flights: Booked in advance (see Flight Bookings section)
- Intercity trains: AC first-class is acceptable
- Intercity buses: Only if travel time <4 hours; AC coach minimum

**Personal Vehicle Usage:**
- If employee uses personal vehicle for business travel, they are reimbursed at INR 8 per km (per company policy)
- Mileage and purpose should be documented with odometer readings

**Ride-Sharing Services:**
- Employees are NOT required to use UberPool, Meru Share, or other shared ride services to save costs
- Premium vs. economy options (e.g., Uber Black) are not covered; use UberX or equivalent

