## 5. Expense Categories and Reimbursement

### 5.1 Reimbursable Expenses

The following business expenses are reimbursable:

**Transportation:**
- Flight tickets (economy, as per policy)
- Train tickets (AC first-class)
- Taxi/cab services to/from airport and for business meetings
- Parking fees during business travel
- Toll charges for company vehicle use

**Accommodation:**
- Hotel room charges (as per budget guidelines)
- Hotel taxes and service charges (included in hotel bill)

**Meals:**
- Per diem allowance (fixed daily amount, no receipts required)
- Client entertainment meals (with business justification) up to INR 5,000 per meal
- Team meals during work-related travel (with receipts)

**Communication:**
- International roaming charges (company cover up to INR 500; balance employee responsibility)
- WiFi in hotel/airport (reasonable charges, typically included in hotel)

**Business Services:**
- Visa fees for international travel
- Travel insurance (mandatory for international trips >5 days)
- Registration fees for conferences or business events
- Printing/copying for business documents

**Other:**
- Portable WiFi rental for remote work during travel (if necessary)
- Business center services (e.g., video conferencing setup in hotel)

### 5.2 Non-Reimbursable Expenses

The following expenses are **NOT reimbursed**:

- Flights/trains booked in Premium/Business class without pre-approval
- Personal travel (spouse, family accompanying, separate tickets)
- Personal entertainment (movies, TV, spa, gym in hotel)
- Personal shopping or gifts
- Alcohol beyond a single beer/wine per meal
- Speeding fines, traffic violations, parking violations
- Travel cancellation charges (preventable through planning)
- Travel insurance premium (if not business travel-related)
- Personal health/wellness products
- Luggage fees for checked baggage (unless required for business equipment)
- Taxi/cab rides for personal errands

