## 11. Travel Safety and Duty of Care

### 11.1 Employee Responsibilities

Employees are responsible for:
- Researching destination safety and health advisories
- Registering with the company before international travel (provide itinerary and emergency contact)
- Maintaining travel insurance during the entire trip
- Keeping manager/HR updated on travel status
- Reporting any safety incidents immediately
- Complying with local laws and regulations

### 11.2 Company Support

The company:
- Provides travel insurance for international trips
- Maintains 24/7 emergency contact line (HR manager on call)
- Covers emergency medical expenses during travel
- Assists with emergency evacuation if necessary (covered by insurance)
- Supports employees in case of travel disruptions (flight cancellations, natural disasters)

### 11.3 High-Risk Destinations

For travel to high-risk regions (defined annually by HR based on government advisories):
- Pre-approval required from the CEO (not just VP)
- Mandatory travel insurance
- Daily check-in with HR required
- Documented security briefing with the manager

**Restricted Regions (No travel authorized):**
- Countries under government travel bans
- Active conflict zones
- Regions with severe pandemic/health emergencies

