## 13. Tax Implications

### 13.1 Travel Allowance Taxation

- Per diem allowances are subject to income tax if they exceed prescribed limits under the Income Tax Act
- Reimbursement of actual expenses (flights, hotels) is generally not taxable
- The Finance team issues tax guidance at year-end for tax filing

### 13.2 GST on Travel Expenses

- GST (18% on some services, 5% on airline tickets) is typically included in vendor pricing
- No separate GST reimbursement is provided to employees (company absorbs GST)

