## 14. Policy Violations and Consequences

### 14.1 Travel Policy Violations

Examples of violations:
- Booking non-approved travel class (e.g., business class without approval)
- Inflating expense claims or submitting false receipts
- Using company travel for personal purposes
- Failing to seek pre-approval before travel
- Submitting expenses >60 days after travel

### 14.2 Consequences

- First violation: Written warning and requirement to refund non-compliant expense
- Repeated violations: Escalation to HR and possible disciplinary action
- Fraudulent claims (false receipts, inflated amounts): Termination and legal action

