## 15. Frequently Asked Questions

**Q: Can I book a flight for a lower price if I fly 1 day earlier and return 1 day later?**  
A: Yes, if the additional hotel nights are less expensive than the flight price difference. Submit justification with the travel request, and manager/VP can approve if it reduces overall cost.

**Q: What if my flight gets cancelled and I have to book a new flight?**  
A: The company covers the cost of the replacement flight. Provide evidence of the cancellation (airline email, booking confirmation) and new ticket receipt in your reimbursement claim.

**Q: Can I use my personal credit card and get reimbursed instead of using the company travel portal?**  
A: Yes, many employees do this. Keep all receipts and submit within 30 days. Reimbursement is processed the same way.

**Q: Is WiFi in the airport/hotel covered?**  
A: WiFi charges are typically included in the hotel room rate or airport access. If separately charged, amounts under INR 300 are usually reimbursed.

**Q: What if I need to travel for a personal emergency (family illness) during work? Is it covered?**  
A: Personal emergency travel is not a business expense; it's your personal responsibility. However, if the manager approves taking leave and subsidizes your travel as a company gesture, this can be arranged on a case-by-case basis.

**Q: Can I claim mileage if I drive my own car for client meetings?**  
A: Yes, personal vehicle usage for business is reimbursed at INR 8 per km. Document the purpose, starting point, destination, and odometer readings.

